-- חוק יסודות התקציב, התשמ"ה-1985 — section 29: a budgeted or supported
-- body may change wages, or grant another monetary benefit tied to work,
-- only as agreed or practised for all state employees or with the Finance
-- Minister's approval, and an agreement or arrangement against that is void
-- to the extent it departs. Sections 21 and 32 say which bodies those are.
-- The text is laws/budget-foundations-law.toml, pinned from the live page
-- of ספר החוקים הפתוח; the corpus holds no copy (MMS-528).
--
-- Why it is here: a circular that pays more than the agreement it carries
-- out stands under section 22 of the Collective Agreements Law
-- (instruments.favourable-circular), and section 29 is what can void that
-- excess where the employer is a budgeted or supported body — the owners
-- of the upper-division schools are. So the amount a contract term gives
-- passes through `the amount that stands under section 29` first.

IMPORT prelude

§ `חוק יסודות התקציב — שינויים בשכר בגוף מתוקצב ובגוף נתמך`

-- What employs the teacher, as far as these sections tell bodies apart.
-- A corporation in section 21's sense is decided by its own law, and a
-- supported body by the Finance Minister's notice in Reshumot (section 32),
-- so which one an employer is, is an input.
DECLARE `employing body` IS ONE OF
    `the State`
    `a corporation`
    `a local authority`
    `a religious council`
    `the Bank of Israel`
    `a government company`
    `a municipal company`
    `a body declared supported`
    `another employer`

§§ `21`

-- "גוף מתוקצב": a corporation, a local authority, a religious council, the
-- Bank of Israel, a government company and a municipal company. The other
-- definitions of the section (a corporation, a health corporation, a year,
-- the excess amount, the kinds of company, the minister concerned) decide
-- matters this encoding takes as inputs or does not use.
@ref law:21
GIVEN b IS AN `employing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a budgeted body` b IF
        b EQUALS `a corporation`
    OR b EQUALS `a local authority`
    OR b EQUALS `a religious council`
    OR b EQUALS `the Bank of Israel`
    OR b EQUALS `a government company`
    OR b EQUALS `a municipal company`

#ASSERT `is a budgeted body` `a local authority`
#ASSERT NOT `is a budgeted body` `the State`

§§ `29`

-- (a) A budgeted or supported body does not agree to, or put in practice,
-- a change in wages, retirement terms or pensions, or another monetary
-- benefit tied to work, except as agreed or practised for all state
-- employees or with the Finance Minister's approval. (The Minister's power
-- to exempt a mixed company on its sale, with the committee's approval, is
-- an input no employer here has: `exempted by the Finance Minister`.)
@ref law:29
GIVEN b IS AN `employing body`
      `as agreed or practised for all state employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by the Finance Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exempted by the Finance Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 29 permits the change` b `as agreed or practised for all state employees` `approved by the Finance Minister` `exempted by the Finance Minister` IF
        NOT `is bound by section 29` b
    OR `as agreed or practised for all state employees`
    OR `approved by the Finance Minister`
    OR `exempted by the Finance Minister`

GIVEN b IS AN `employing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is bound by section 29` b IF
        `is a budgeted body` b
    OR `is a supported body` b

-- (b) Notwithstanding any law, an agreement or arrangement is void to the
-- extent it is contrary to (a): of what it gives, what (a) permits stands
-- and the excess is void. `the amount section 29 permits` is what was
-- agreed or practised for all state employees, which is an input.
GIVEN `the amount agreed or arranged` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount section 29 permits` IS A NUMBER
      `the change is permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount that stands under section 29` `the amount agreed or arranged` `the amount section 29 permits` `the change is permitted` IS
    IF `the change is permitted`
    THEN `the amount agreed or arranged`
    ELSE min `the amount agreed or arranged` `the amount section 29 permits`

-- (c) and (d): what the Finance Minister may do when a body does not
-- comply — deduct the amount paid from what the State transfers to it, stop
-- or reduce a grant — and what a director or director-general who agreed
-- knowingly is taken to have done. They act on the body, not on what the
-- teacher is paid, so no rule here.

#ASSERT `section 29 permits the change` `the State` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 29 permits the change` `a local authority` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 29 permits the change` `a local authority` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 29 permits the change` `a body declared supported` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the amount that stands under section 29` 481 480.77 TRUE EQUALS 481
#ASSERT `the amount that stands under section 29` 481 480.77 FALSE EQUALS 480.77
#ASSERT `the amount that stands under section 29` 470 480.77 FALSE EQUALS 470

§§ `32`

-- "גוף נתמך": a corporation whose budget the government takes part in,
-- directly or indirectly, and which the Finance Minister has declared a
-- supported body for this Law by notice in Reshumot. Whether an owner of
-- schools is one is the notice's, an input: `a body declared supported`.
@ref law:32
GIVEN b IS AN `employing body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a supported body` b IF
    b EQUALS `a body declared supported`

#ASSERT `is a supported body` `a body declared supported`
#ASSERT NOT `is a supported body` `another employer`
